# Rethinking the Civil War Era

**Authors:** Paul D. Escott

## Abstract
<p>The field of Civil War history seems to have reached an inflection point. There is a great amount of interesting new research that departs from long-established channels and seems to be looking in new directions. This volume examines much of the latest work. It covers the sectional crisis, the war itself, and concepts of the Civil War era. Although not a conventional historiography, it offers broad coverage of the field, raises major interpretive questions, and suggests many new issues or questions to research.</p>

**Source:** https://doi.org/10.5810/kentucky/9780813175355.001.0001

